%% TARGET DESIGN. GL0 uses chain consensus, not a global BFT round.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as CL1 / DL1
    participant M as ML0
    participant A as GL0 admission committee
    participant E as GL0 execution committee
    participant G as GL0 producer
    participant F as ordinary GL0 followers
    participant W as selected noncommittee watchtowers

    C->>M: submit framework-economic or custom-data block
    M->>M: metagraph snapshot consensus
    M->>A: signed state-channel binary
    A->>A: per-binary secret VRF admission and authentication
    A->>E: buffer binary in static execution shard
    E->>E: scheduled producer pins exact Phase-2 base and pre-root
    E->>E: replay exact ordered CL1 inputs and compute canonical diff and root
    E->>E: build checkpoint committing inputs, diff, root, base, and ancestry
    E->>E: every signer independently replays and signs only identical diff and root
    E->>G: checkpoint with distinct execution threshold
    G->>G: verify threshold, exact base and pre-root CAS, continuity, namespace
    G->>G: apply scoped diff, recompute root, embed in global snapshot
    G->>F: signed global snapshot
    F->>F: repeat adoption checks, apply scoped diff, and recompute root
    E-->>W: checkpoint inputs, diff, root, and execution certificate
    W->>W: independently replay for collusion detection
    Note over E,W: Watchtower release and adjudication timing is an open protocol decision
    F-->>M: exact Phase-2 canonical GL0 state
    F-->>C: exact Phase-2 canonical GL0 state

    Note over E,F: Execution threshold is required for diff adoption. Shard depth selects the checkpoint chain and cannot replace missing executions.
